1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,742
Zen Analytics Workbench —
chapter one: orientation.

2
00:00:03,802 --> 00:00:07,346
One model of a distributed
system, seen five ways.

3
00:00:07,406 --> 00:00:10,436
The lenses live across the top of the window.

4
00:00:10,496 --> 00:00:14,640
Logical is what the system does:
services, and the data between them.

5
00:00:14,700 --> 00:00:18,159
Physical is where it runs.

6
00:00:18,219 --> 00:00:24,661
Edge, on-prem and Azure are drawn as domains
— and every link that crosses one has a price.

7
00:00:24,721 --> 00:00:28,235
Network is how it is wired.

8
00:00:28,295 --> 00:00:34,738
Protocol, port and bandwidth on each
link, with per-domain egress and exposure.

9
00:00:34,798 --> 00:00:38,843
Racks is the same design as hardware.

10
00:00:38,903 --> 00:00:45,848
Real machines in real rack units, with
power, heat, weight and floor area budgeted.

11
00:00:45,908 --> 00:00:49,913
Code is the repository that implements it.

12
00:00:49,973 --> 00:00:56,920
Symbols, files and calls, indexed from the
source — chapter ten covers this lens in full.

13
00:00:56,980 --> 00:01:00,223
Back to Logical.

14
00:01:00,283 --> 00:01:04,426
One model. Five viewpoints.
Nothing is redrawn by hand.

15
00:01:04,486 --> 00:01:07,935
Designs are kept as workspaces.

16
00:01:07,995 --> 00:01:14,438
The switcher holds as many as you like —
new, duplicate, rename, import, export.

17
00:01:14,498 --> 00:01:21,044
Push the whole set to the backend,
or pull it down on another machine.

18
00:01:21,104 --> 00:01:23,642
Under the title bar sit the three
inputs everything is computed against.

19
00:01:23,702 --> 00:01:28,337
RECORDS — how much data the system holds.

20
00:01:28,397 --> 00:01:33,022
QUERIES PER DAY — how hard it is asked.

21
00:01:33,082 --> 00:01:36,424
And SKEW — how unevenly that load lands.

22
00:01:36,484 --> 00:01:41,717
Move one, and the whole model recomputes.

23
00:01:41,777 --> 00:01:52,221
Cost per month, storage, issues, network
findings — all of it live, at the bottom.

24
00:01:52,281 --> 00:02:03,291
Bottlenecks, Costs, Network, Events, Capacity
— and Ask, for a question in plain English.

25
00:02:03,351 --> 00:02:06,385
On the left is the catalog you build from.

26
00:02:06,445 --> 00:02:13,258
Services on one tab, field
devices on the other.

27
00:02:13,318 --> 00:02:20,835
Filter it to Azure, to open source, or to AWS.

28
00:02:20,895 --> 00:02:24,037
Everything you see here is computed.

29
00:02:24,097 --> 00:02:27,701
Nothing on this canvas is decoration.
